 "intro_html": "Korea's post-war comfort stew: tinned luncheon meat, sausages and baked beans meet kimchi and instant noodles, with a slice of cheese melting on top. It is traditionally cooked in a <b>wide, shallow pan</b> in the middle of the table, so a steel sauté pan is ideal. The ingredients are arranged in sections, broth is poured around them and the noodles go in last. This version is <b>mild</b>: gochujang only, no chilli flakes. The heat comes from your <a href=\"kimchi.html\">kimchi</a>, and you can control it. Beef luncheon meat and beef frankfurters (common in Turkey) work well. This is a home adaptation built from several Korean sources and has not been kitchen tested.",
