 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>The sauce here has no chilli flakes, so the only heat comes from the kimchi.</li><li>For a very mild pot, use less kimchi or squeeze out its juice.</li><li>Classic budae jjigae uses <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">1–2 tbsp</span> gochugaru.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "How spicy it gets"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Pork Spam can be hard to find; tinned beef luncheon meat (dana jambon or dana luncheon) and beef frankfurters (dana sosis) taste close.</li><li>Sucuk is too strongly spiced and greasy for this stew.</li><li>Any baked beans in tomato sauce work.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "What to use in Turkey"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Use only the noodle block; keep the seasoning packet aside or add a quarter of it if the broth tastes flat.</li><li>Korean ramyeon noodles hold up best, but any instant noodle works.</li><li>Add more stock and a second block to stretch it for 4 people.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Ramen"
  }
 ],
